-- dispatch (core): a `foreign type` never gets a derived row (A.55).
--
-- `Key` is `equatable`, so `==` on a `Hidden` resolves — §3.4 says the
-- marker means exactly "has an `eq`" and it is the bridge core leans on
-- until §5.2. What answers it is `Basics.eq`, the one structural walk in
-- `core/Basics.js`; the table writes it as the `undetermined`
-- leaf, which `Lower` reads off the derived ancestor as `Basics.eq`
-- (checker-v2.md §12.2).
--
-- What must NOT be here is a `derived eq M.Key` row: a `foreign type` has
-- no constructors to walk, so that row would name a function the backend
-- has nothing to emit for. The golden's whole job is the row that is absent.
pub equatable foreign type Key


pub opaque type Hidden
    = Hidden Key


pub same : Hidden, Hidden -> Bool
same a b =
    a == b
